				<wikidot:authorName>sirpudding</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>348648</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Yeah, maybe as a Project Thor, &quot;crowbars from God&quot; kinetic kill satellite network. I think I would have liked an article about such a system under the Centre's control, with a mention of the alternate SCP-169 as a contingency target. You'd lose the image, but perhaps SPC-001 requires that the penetrators themselves be sculpted as fists. I think this article makes that article impossible though, unfortunately.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1714644#post-2512239</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1714644/spc-169-j#post-2512239</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 21 May 2016 02:21:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>daveyoufool</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2034230</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I get what you're saying and I appreciate your honesty. However (though it pains me to do so from a humor writing standpoint) I feel like I should offer a bit of explanation for the joke for the sake of clarity.</p> <p>The joke is not that the Shark Punching Center exists. The joke is that they adhere to their mission so blindly and closed-mindedly that they're willing to awaken SCP-169 and destroy human civilization, just so that they can complete their duty to punch every shark (and everything that might be interpreted as a shark even metaphorically) in existence.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1714644#post-2512233</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1714644/spc-169-j#post-2512233</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 21 May 2016 02:13:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dr Hysteria</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1595697</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I didn't like it.</p> <p>The whole article is just riding off of the success of another skip and I don't even understand what the joke is. Is it funny because they wanna punch <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-169">SCP-169</a>? Is it humorous because they think <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-169">SCP-169</a> is a shark? Is it farcical because one of the characters said a swear word? Is it because they overreact in extremely absurd ways? Because apparently that joke hasn't been milked dry yet. Granted the image made me smirk but it feels as if the entire comedic basis for this piece is just saying that the Shark Punching Center exists and they're silly.</p> <p>Somehow common knowledge is funny now.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
